<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roger de Montgomery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1094">1094</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Roger of Montgomery, Roger de Montgomery, 1st Earl of Shrewsbury</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roger de Montgomery was a Norman noble and close adviser of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>. Made Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a> around 1074, he built castles at Shrewsbury and at Montgomery, which took its name from his Norman home, and led Norman expansion into mid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> and Powys. He founded Shrewsbury Abbey, where he was buried in 1094.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roger-de-montgomery.jpg" alt="Roger de Montgomery" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_famille_fr_de_Montgommery.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
